 "etapas": [
  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The soft «c» and the hard «c»",
     "texto": [
      "Before **a, o, u**, the «c» sounds hard /k/, like the «c» in «cat»: **casa**, **come**, **ascolta**.",
      "Before **e, i**, the «c» sounds soft /tʃ/, exactly like the «ch» in «church»: **cena** (read «CHEH-nah»), **cinema** (read «CHEE-neh-mah»), **dieci** (read «DYEH-chee»).",
      "To keep the strong /k/ sound before e, i, a silent «h» is added: **chi** (read «kee»), **che** (read «keh»), **amiche** (read «ah-MEE-keh»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The combinations cia, cio, ciu",
     "texto": [
      "When you see **cia**, **cio** or **ciu**, the «i» is not pronounced as a separate vowel: it only shows that the «c» sounds soft, like «ch». That's why **ciao** is read «chow» and **cioccolato** is read «chohk-koh-LAH-toh»."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
